---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Plenivostudio is an independent maker of offline digital planning tools — one-time purchase software that keeps your data on your device."
  path="/about"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 760px;">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal="up">About</p>
      <h1 data-reveal="up">Software made to be owned, not rented</h1>
      <p class="lead" data-reveal="up">
        {site.brandName} is a small, independent maker of digital planning tools —
        files you buy once and keep. No subscriptions, no accounts, no cloud
        services standing between you and your plans.
      </p>
      <p data-reveal="up">
        Our first product, the Ultimate Offline Life Planner, is a single
        self-contained HTML file. It runs in your browser, works without an
        internet connection, and stores your data locally on your own device.
        When you are done planning, you can export everything to a file you
        control.
      </p>

      <h2 data-reveal="up">What we believe</h2>
      <ul class="beliefs" data-reveal="up">
        <li>
          <strong>Ownership over access.</strong> When you pay for software, you
          should own a copy of it — not rent permission to use it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Privacy by architecture.</strong> The simplest way to protect
          your data is to never collect it. Our planner has no analytics, no
          tracking and no network calls.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Honesty over marketing.</strong> We state what our software
          does, what it requires, and where its limits are — on this site and in
          the documentation included with every product.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 data-reveal="up">A note on legal details</h2>
      <p data-reveal="up">
        Checkout is not live yet. Before it goes live, we will publish our full
        legal company details here — company name, registered address and
        governing jurisdiction. We do not use placeholder company names or
        fictional addresses, and we do not invent registration or tax details.
      </p>

      <p data-reveal="up">
        Questions? <a href="/contact">Contact us</a> — we read every message.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .lead {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink, #16181d);
  }
  .container p,
  .container li {
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .container h2 {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  .beliefs {
    padding-left: 1.4rem;
  }
  .beliefs li + li {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }
</style>
